Several Markdown files print one outline each, separated by a blank line; a number in frontmatter like `version: 2` prints unquoted, and a `#` line inside a fenced code block isn't a heading.
== args
input/doc-with-frontmatter.md
input/doc-headings-only.md
input/doc-with-code.md
input/regular.md
== file input/doc-with-frontmatter.md
---
title: 'API Documentation'
version: 2
---

# Introduction

## Getting Started
== file input/doc-headings-only.md
# Overview
Some description here.
## Details
== file input/doc-with-code.md
# Configuration

```yaml
# This is not a heading
setting: value
```

## Options
== file input/regular.md
# config
